1. Vijay Singh
2. Rahul Sharma
3. Suresh Kumar                                       … Accused / Applicants

APPLICATION UNDER SECTION 227 OF THE BHARATIYA NAGARIK SURAKSHA SANHITA, 2023
FOR DISCHARGE OF THE ACCUSED

MOST RESPECTFULLY SHOWETH:

1. That the applicants are innocent and have been falsely implicated in the present case due to business rivalry.

2. That the prosecution has filed a chargesheet under Sections 302, 120B and 201 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023.

3. That even if the entire prosecution material is taken at its face value, no prima facie case is made out against the applicants for the offences charged.

4. GROUNDS FOR DISCHARGE

A. There is no direct evidence of conspiracy. The alleged conspiracy meeting is not supported by any independent witness. The witness claiming to have seen the meeting is an interested party.

B. The mobile call records merely show that the applicants were in communication. This does not establish conspiracy. Communication between business partners is normal and does not prove criminal conspiracy.

C. There is no eye-witness to the murder. The entire case rests on circumstantial evidence which is weak and does not form a complete chain.

D. The weapon recovery is suspicious. There were no independent witnesses to the recovery. The seizure memo is not reliable.

E. The DNA evidence is affected by chain of custody issues. The samples were not properly preserved, affecting their reliability.

F. The allegation of destruction of evidence is not supported by any direct evidence. No one saw the applicants destroying evidence.

G. Business rivalry alone cannot establish conspiracy or motive for murder. Many businesses have rivalries without criminal incidents.

5. That the ingredients of Section 120B BNS (criminal conspiracy) are not made out. There is no evidence of agreement to commit murder.

6. That continuing the criminal proceedings against the applicants would be an abuse of the process of law.

PRAYER

It is therefore most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble Court may be pleased to:

(a) Discharge all the applicants from the charges under Sections 302, 120B and 201 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023;
(b) Pass any other order as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper.

